{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790256131,"nonce":"FldQuxTENtwT4VZGN9QlrCX5Yeo=","title":"Lua: Complex.new in mandelbrot is an untyped field-function call, so nothing sinks","message":"mandelbrot.lua wins on the Mac (LuaJIT 170 ms) but loses about 6x on the NUC (LuaJIT's x86 float code is fast). The inner loop constructs a Complex per step through Complex.new, a field-function call the typer does not resolve, so allocation sinking (C-sink-merges) never sees the constructor. Resolve field-function calls on class tables through the which-finder machinery (L-which-finders) and type the result as the class's shape.","files":null}]}